  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"44\" data-end=\"294\"><strong data-start=\"44\" data-end=\"54\">Leptin</strong> is a hormone primarily produced by <strong data-start=\"90\" data-end=\"114\">adipose (fat) tissue</strong>. It plays a crucial role in regulating <strong data-start=\"154\" data-end=\"194\">appetite, energy balance, metabolism</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"215\">body weight</strong> by signaling the brain (especially the hypothalamus) about fat storage levels.</p>\n<table style=\"width: 91.0876%;\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 39.9456%;\"><strong>Group</strong></th>\n<th style=\"width: 59.9184%;\"><strong>Leptin Level (ng/mL)</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.9456%;\"><strong>Men</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 59.9184%;\">0.5 &ndash; 12 ng/mL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.9456%;\"><strong>Women</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 59.9184%;\">3 &ndash; 25 ng/mL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.9456%;\"><strong>Obese individuals</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 59.9184%;\">Can exceed <strong>40&ndash;100+ ng/mL</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1570\"><strong data-start=\"1545\" data-end=\"1570\">Key Clinical Contexts</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1572\" data-end=\"1591\"><strong data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1591\">1. Obesity</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1592\" data-end=\"1843\">\n<li data-start=\"1592\" data-end=\"1647\">\n<p data-start=\"1594\" data-end=\"1647\">Leptin levels are <strong data-start=\"1612\" data-end=\"1620\">high</strong>, proportional to fat mass.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1648\" data-end=\"1774\">\n<p data-start=\"1650\" data-end=\"1774\">However, many obese individuals develop <strong data-start=\"1690\" data-end=\"1711\">leptin resistance</strong>, where the brain fails to respond to leptin's satiety signals.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1775\" data-end=\"1843\">\n<p data-start=\"1777\" data-end=\"1843\">High leptin in obesity <strong data-start=\"1800\" data-end=\"1842\">does not suppress appetite effectively</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1845\" data-end=\"1874\"><strong data-start=\"1850\" data-end=\"1874\">2. Leptin Deficiency</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1875\" data-end=\"2062\">\n<li data-start=\"1875\" data-end=\"1910\">\n<p data-start=\"1877\" data-end=\"1910\">Extremely rare genetic condition.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1911\" data-end=\"2002\">\n<p data-start=\"1913\" data-end=\"2002\">Presents with <strong data-start=\"1927\" data-end=\"1957\">severe early-onset obesity</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1959\" data-end=\"1974\">hyperphagia</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"1980\" data-end=\"2001\">low leptin levels</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2003\" data-end=\"2062\">\n<p data-start=\"2005\" data-end=\"2062\">Can be treated with <strong data-start=\"2025\" data-end=\"2061\">recombinant leptin (metreleptin)</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"2064\" data-end=\"2118\"><strong data-start=\"2069\" data-end=\"2118\">3. Hypothalamic Amenorrhea / Anorexia Nervosa</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2119\" data-end=\"2286\">\n<li data-start=\"2119\" data-end=\"2179\">\n<p data-start=\"2121\" data-end=\"2179\">Very <strong data-start=\"2126\" data-end=\"2140\">low leptin</strong> levels due to insufficient fat stores.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2180\" data-end=\"2286\">\n<p data-start=\"2182\" data-end=\"2286\">May result in <strong data-start=\"2196\" data-end=\"2248\">suppressed gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH)</strong>, leading to menstrual irregularities.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"2288\" data-end=\"2313\"><strong data-start=\"2293\" data-end=\"2313\">4. Lipodystrophy</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2314\" data-end=\"2489\">\n<li data-start=\"2314\" data-end=\"2450\">\n<p data-start=\"2316\" data-end=\"2450\">Characterized by <strong data-start=\"2333\" data-end=\"2362\">abnormal fat distribution</strong> and often <strong data-start=\"2373\" data-end=\"2394\">low leptin levels</strong> despite insulin resistance and metabolic complications.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2451\" data-end=\"2489\">\n<p data-start=\"2453\" data-end=\"2489\">May benefit from <strong data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2488\">leptin therapy</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
